# DashTab Backend — Cursor Rules

## Architecture
- Dependency direction: Domain → Application → Infrastructure → API
- Domain has zero external dependencies (no EF Core, no packages)
- Application holds interfaces and DTOs only — no implementations
- Infrastructure holds EF Core DbContext, service implementations, and seeding
- API holds controllers and Program.cs only — no business logic in controllers

## Project Structure
- Entities → DashTab.Domain/Entities/
- Enums → DashTab.Domain/Enums/
- Exceptions → DashTab.Domain/Exceptions/
- DTOs and request models → DashTab.Application/Dtos/
- Service interfaces → DashTab.Application/Interfaces/
- Service implementations → DashTab.Infrastructure/Services/
- Controllers → DashTab.API/Controllers/

## Entities
- Plain classes with data annotations ([Key], [Required], [MaxLength], [Column])
- No abstract base classes
- Navigation properties use = null! for required and ? for optional
- Collections initialized with = []

## Services
- Constructor-inject AppDbContext directly — no repository pattern
- Keep all business logic inside services, never in controllers
- Return DTOs from services, never raw entities
- Set CreatedAt and UpdatedAt manually when creating or updating

## Controllers
- Thin — only call a service method and return the result
- Use IActionResult return type
- Map exceptions to HTTP status codes in try/catch (400, 404, 422)
- Routes follow the pattern: api/v1/<resource>

## DTOs
- Use records for DTOs and request models
- One file per feature group (e.g. OrderDto.cs, StaffDtos.cs)

## EF Core
- Use AppDbContext directly in services
- Configure relationships in OnModelCreating — no separate configuration classes
- Use HasConversion<string>() for enums stored as strings
- Use numeric(10,2) for all money/price columns

## Naming
- Files: PascalCase (OrderService.cs)
- Classes: PascalCase
- Methods: PascalCase
- Variables and parameters: camelCase
- Database columns: snake_case (via EFCore.NamingConventions)

## General
- No business logic in controllers
- No raw entities returned from controllers
- No repository pattern — services use DbContext directly
- Keep code simple and readable — avoid unnecessary abstractions
